      "content": "hey, i'm dealing with a really weird issue in our gke cluster. i have this one microservice that keeps hitting a CrashLoopBackOff, but the timing is totally unpredictable. it'll run fine for hours, then suddenly just die for no apparent reason, and then it'll come back up and work perfectly again for a while. \n\nthe logs are basically useless—just a bunch of generic errors that don't point to any specific fault. it feels like the error is just popping up and disappearing randomly. can u give me a checklist of what i should look at to track down why this is happening so sporadically?",
